      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. i tried the error handling thing just to see if it would bypass it, and it does work, but it's like a bandage on a bullet wound. the error is still happening, just silently, so we don't actually know what caused it.\n\nthe most frustrating part is that everything is so clean. i've checked for background processes, i've checked for add-ins, and the environment is stable. it's like the error just materializes out of nowhere, performs its little glitch, and then vanishes. it's so random that it almost feels less like a software conflict and more like something is actively, intentionally interfering with the execution at the exact moment the macro hits that line. why would a file just decide to fail one day and then behave perfectly the next?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
